<title>EGYPT: Egypt pound interbank rates soften.</title>
<headline>Egypt pound interbank rates soften.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Overnight interbank rates on the Egyptian pound tended softer on Monday despite some shortage in the private sector market, to between 8-5/8 and 9-1/8 percent from 8-3/4 and 9-3/8 percent on Sunday, bankers said.</p>
<p>&quot;The market was short but not to the extent to push prices up,&quot; said one banker.</p>
<p>One-week rates were also down at between 8-3/4 and nine percent from 8-7/8 and 9-1/8 percent, they added.</p>
<p>$1 = 3.395</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +202 578 3290/91</p>
